cff-version: 1.2.1
title: "kinextract: Non-parametric binned-LOSVD spectral fitter for galaxy kinematics"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Waters
    given-names: Thomas, K.
    affiliation: University of Michigan
version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-02"
url: "https://github.com/thomas-k-waters/kinextract"
abstract: >
  kinextract fits galaxy spectra using a non-parametric line-of-sight velocity
  distribution (LOSVD) represented directly on a velocity grid, for any
  number of template spectra in a single fitting engine. The defaults are
  the recipe validated on NGC 4751 MUSE data: a third-difference roughness
  penalty at a fixed strength, raised for broad LOSVDs and for fits at the
  edge of the velocity grid; a shared multiplicative continuum co-fitted
  with the LOSVD and template weights; and residual-based error inflation
  against sky-line residuals and bad pixels. Uncertainty bands come from
  the Laplace approximation to the posterior with a sky-line and
  template-mismatch variance model, re-centered on the fit, with an
  optional NUTS/NumPyro reference mode. Schwarzschild-model inputs carry
  each velocity bin's posterior scatter. The package targets
  integral-field-spectroscopy data (MUSE, STIS) for black-hole mass
  measurements through Schwarzschild orbit modeling.
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - spectroscopy
  - galaxy kinematics
  - LOSVD
  - Schwarzschild orbit library modeling
license: MIT
